    "['switchport trunk encapsulation [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'port link-type dot1q-tunnel', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nport link-type dot1q-tunnel\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei devices, the equivalent concept to Cisco\\'s \"switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q\" is typically handled by setting the port link-type to dot1q-tunnel (for Q-in-Q tunneling) or trunk (for standard 802.1Q trunking). Since the original Cisco command specifies 802.1Q encapsulation for trunking, the most direct Huawei equivalent would be to configure the port as a trunk port, which inherently uses 802.1Q encapsulation in Huawei devices. \\n\\nHowever, if you specifically need the encapsulation command equivalent, Huawei devices don\\'t have a direct 1:1 command since 802.1Q is the default encapsulation for trunk ports. The closest would be setting the port as a trunk port (which is done with `port link-type trunk`), but since the example shows both access and trunk configurations on the same interface in Cisco (which isn\\'t possible in reality), I\\'ve provided the dot1q-tunnel option which is Huawei\\'s Q-in-Q implementation.\\n\\nFor a standard trunk port in Huawei, you would use:\\n##\\nport link-type trunk\\n##', 'trans_template': 'port link-type dot1q-tunnel'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'port link-type trunk', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nport link-type dot1q-tunnel\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei devices, the equivalent concept to Cisco\\'s \"switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q\" is typically handled by setting the port link-type to dot1q-tunnel (for Q-in-Q tunneling) or trunk (for standard 802.1Q trunking). Since the original Cisco command specifies 802.1Q encapsulation for trunking, the most direct Huawei equivalent would be to configure the port as a trunk port, which inherently uses 802.1Q encapsulation in Huawei devices. \\n\\nHowever, if you specifically need the encapsulation command equivalent, Huawei devices don\\'t have a direct 1:1 command since 802.1Q is the default encapsulation for trunk ports. The closest would be setting the port as a trunk port (which is done with `port link-type trunk`), but since the example shows both access and trunk configurations on the same interface in Cisco (which isn\\'t possible in reality), I\\'ve provided the dot1q-tunnel option which is Huawei\\'s Q-in-Q implementation.\\n\\nFor a standard trunk port in Huawei, you would use:\\n##\\nport link-type trunk\\n##', 'trans_template': 'port link-type trunk'}]]": 1,
